<title>UK: TABLE-BPB change to accounting ups profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BPB change to accounting ups profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to  March 31.</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		25.0		   vs 20.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.75		   vs 6.35</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 10.3		   vs 9.7</p>
<p> Pretax		     189.1		  vs 161.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   1.39 billion	 vs 1.423</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 160 and 165 million stg on the old accounting basis.</p>
<p>The above figures reflect a change in accounting procedures in the results to change the translation basis for currencies from using a closing level to an average exchange rate.</p>
<p>The pretax profit figure also includes gains on disposals. Stripping those gains out pretax profits were 178.3 million stg.</p>
<p>Full company name - BPB Industries Plc.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
